      "index": 0,
      "type": "text",
      "weight": 0.2,
      "score": 43,
      "reasoning": "This is an Objective (Mode A) criterion. The report quantitatively summarizes the M33 X-7 posterior using 16th–84th percentile intervals (14.2–17.2 M☉ and 0.78–0.89), sample count, and correlation, but it does not provide the explicitly required marginalized mean ± standard deviation for either mass or spin; quantiles are not necessarily equivalent for non-Gaussian posteriors."
     },
     {
      "index": 1,
      "type": "image",
      "weight": 0.3,
      "score": 43,
      "reasoning": "Mode A. The report computes the required Monte Carlo posterior-mass probability versus boson mass and includes the 0.05 threshold; its M33 X-7 curve has the correct broad trough and comparable lower edge. However, the scan is truncated near 10^-11 eV rather than extending to 10^-10 eV, the upper exclusion edge and intermediate structure differ noticeably from the target, and the published n≤6/uncorrected/box comparisons are not faithfully reproduced."
     },
     {
      "index": 2,
      "type": "text",
      "weight": 0.5,
      "score": 18,
      "reasoning": "Mode A. The report provides quantitative 95% self-interaction boundaries for M33 X-7 in terms of the decay constant f and mass intervals, but never defines or reports the requested upper limit on g in GeV⁻¹ or explicitly establishes the conversion between f and g. Moreover, the limit relies on an acknowledged phenomenological bosenova prescription, so it cannot be directly compared with the published g constraint."
     }
    ],
